# Easy Key Lime Pie Bars

Based on [Sally’s Baking Addiction](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/key-lime-pie-bars/)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 12 [full-sheet graham crackers]{ ing="full-sheet-graham-crackers" } (yields 1.5 cups/180g crumbs)
- [ ] 6 Tbsps (85g) [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, melted
- [ ] 1/4 cup (50g) [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 4 ounces (113g) [full-fat brick cream cheese]{ ing="full-fat-brick-cream-cheese" }, softened
- [ ] 4 large [egg yolks]{ ing="egg-yolks" }
- [ ] 14-ounce (397g) can [sweetened condensed milk]{ ing="sweetened-condensed-milk" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup (120ml) [key lime juice]{ ing="key-lime-juice" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [lime zest]{ ing="lime-zest" } (about 1 lime or 2 key limes)
- [ ] Optional garnish: [whipped cream]{ ing="whipped-cream" } and [lime slices]{ ing="lime-slices" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350°F. Line 9-inch square pan with parchment paper, leaving overhang for easy removal.
1. Grind [graham crackers]{ ing="full-sheet-graham-crackers" } into fine crumbs. Mix crumbs with [sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }, then stir in melted [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }. Press mixture into pan bottom.
1. Prebake crust for 10 minutes, then cool briefly.
1. Beat softened [cream cheese]{ ing="full-fat-brick-cream-cheese" } until smooth. Add [egg yolks]{ ing="egg-yolks" } and beat. Mix in condensed milk, [key lime juice]{ ing="key-lime-juice" }, and [lime zest]{ ing="lime-zest" }. Hand-whisk to remove any lumps, then pour over warm crust.
1. Bake 18-20 minutes until edges are set and center is slightly jiggly.
1. Cool 30 minutes at room temperature, then refrigerate at least 2-3 hours.
1. Lift parchment from pan and cut into squares. Garnish with whipped cream, [lime slices]{ ing="lime-slices" }, or [zest]{ ing="lime-zest" }.

## Notes

- Keeps up to 5 days in airtight refrigerated container.
